@flexiarg problems/satisfied-rungs-are-counted-and-surfaced
@title Satisfied Rungs Are Counted and Surfaced
@style pattern
@why war-room/wr-25-good-news-gets-the-same-evidence-discipline-as-bad
@holds-at R5

! conclusion: Count and surface a satisfied rung with the same evidence discipline used for an unsatisfied rung.

  + context: Red ring at R5, ruling WR-25, established 2026-08-22 in
    p4ng/empirics-futon/wr-overlay.edn. Supplied by M-aif-faithfulness and
    M-war-machine-aif-completion, which put earned rungs on the War Machine
    evidence surface.
    + salience: 香. `:warm-customer-pays` is the strongest signal the outside
      world can send this stack — someone paid — and it arrived satisfied,
      uncounted and unsurfaced. M-futon-problems records the same instance as
      G2, "which problems the world cared about", alongside cold-ladder titles
      reading n=0 over positions n=1-2 and `:position` absent from the
      projection the machine steers by. The gap is therefore not that a counter
      is missing. It is that the one verdict the apparatus cannot issue to
      itself was received and not perceived, so nothing downstream could
      compose with it (futon-theory/futonic-logic, A7: without salience,
      generativity remains inert).
    + whose problem: the operator's, and through him the paying party's. This
      is the one red ring of the five whose cost is borne outside the stack.

  + IF:
    A rung such as `:warm-customer-pays` becomes satisfied.

  + HOWEVER:
    The satisfied rung is uncounted and unsurfaced, so good news does not receive the same discipline as bad news.

  + THEN:
    Add satisfied rungs to the counted evidence projection and surface their supporting artifact without changing a numerical posterior unless that artifact warrants the change.

  + BECAUSE:
    A rung stays earned only when its satisfying evidence remains visible and auditable under the same rule applied to adverse evidence.
    ?evidence(required): No source row demonstrates a live projection that counts and surfaces `:warm-customer-pays`.
